{
  "case_id": "2017-17-965",
  "document_hash": "9a3d677bf59b0404b8933f001905d773fd9974778efe8dcbb9d5dd5b5f97c90e",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2017-17-965",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "9a3d677bf59b0404b8933f001905d773fd9974778efe8dcbb9d5dd5b5f97c90e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9a3d677bf59b-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: You -- you\nmentioned 1182(f). And the worrisome thing\nabout this is that the President acts; Congress\nis the one responsible for making the laws\nabout immigration. It has been suggested in\none of the briefs that we read 1182(f) to allow\nthe President to suspend entry but only for a\nperiod of time long enough for Congress to say\nyea or nay."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2017-17-965",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "9a3d677bf59b0404b8933f001905d773fd9974778efe8dcbb9d5dd5b5f97c90e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9a3d677bf59b-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Why not an\nEstablishment Clause claim?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2017-17-965",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9a3d677bf59b0404b8933f001905d773fd9974778efe8dcbb9d5dd5b5f97c90e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9a3d677bf59b-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "General, today, can we go back to something that's been bothering me here, which is -- and it was argued in a case this week about the unitary executive theory, which basically says the President is at the head, I think -- I'm summarizing in an incomplete way"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Neal K. Katyal",
      "case_id": "2017-17-965",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9a3d677bf59b0404b8933f001905d773fd9974778efe8dcbb9d5dd5b5f97c90e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9a3d677bf59b-0001-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The executive order is unlawful for three reasons: It conflicts with Congress's policy choices. It defies the bar on nationality discrimination, something you never heard my friend talk about. And it violates the First Amendment."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Neal K. Katyal",
      "case_id": "2017-17-965",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9a3d677bf59b0404b8933f001905d773fd9974778efe8dcbb9d5dd5b5f97c90e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9a3d677bf59b-0001-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "He could for two reasons. There's two different arguments. There's the nationality discrimination ban, 1152, and then there's, you know, whether or not this comports with Congress's policy judgments."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2017-17-965",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9a3d677bf59b0404b8933f001905d773fd9974778efe8dcbb9d5dd5b5f97c90e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9a3d677bf59b-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, does this proclamation do anything like that? Does this proclamation purport to establish a new permanent immigration policy for the United States?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Katyal",
      "case_id": "2017-17-965",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9a3d677bf59b0404b8933f001905d773fd9974778efe8dcbb9d5dd5b5f97c90e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9a3d677bf59b-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Absolutely, Your Honor. This is a perpetual policy that bans. It does exactly what Congress in 1965 said you can't do."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2017-17-965",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9a3d677bf59b0404b8933f001905d773fd9974778efe8dcbb9d5dd5b5f97c90e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9a3d677bf59b-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 47,
        "start": 47
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I thought it had to be reexamined every 180 days?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Katyal",
      "case_id": "2017-17-965",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9a3d677bf59b0404b8933f001905d773fd9974778efe8dcbb9d5dd5b5f97c90e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9a3d677bf59b-0002-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 47,
        "start": 47
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "No, that's not what it says. It says there's a report that has to come in at 180 days, and nothing happens at the end of the report."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2017-17-965",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9a3d677bf59b0404b8933f001905d773fd9974778efe8dcbb9d5dd5b5f97c90e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9a3d677bf59b-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 55,
        "start": 55
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I -- I guess the question, though, Mr. Katyal, is maybe you're entirely right that 1182(f) needs to have some limits to prevent the President from doing something that's completely contrary to another section of the statute."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Katyal",
      "case_id": "2017-17-965",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9a3d677bf59b0404b8933f001905d773fd9974778efe8dcbb9d5dd5b5f97c90e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9a3d677bf59b-0002-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 55,
        "start": 55
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "That is not our argument."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2017-17-965",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9a3d677bf59b0404b8933f001905d773fd9974778efe8dcbb9d5dd5b5f97c90e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9a3d677bf59b-0003-0003",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 67,
        "start": 67
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "This is a ban that really does fall almost exclusively on Muslims, between 90.2 percent and 99.8 percent Muslims."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2017-17-965",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9a3d677bf59b0404b8933f001905d773fd9974778efe8dcbb9d5dd5b5f97c90e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9a3d677bf59b-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 68,
        "start": 68
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GORSUCH: Mr. Katyal, on that, it's been a long time since this Court has used the Lemon test, reasonable observer, even to strike down a domestic statute, let alone something with purely international application. What -- what do we do about that?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "U.S. Conference of Catholic Bishops",
      "case_id": "2017-17-965",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9a3d677bf59b0404b8933f001905d773fd9974778efe8dcbb9d5dd5b5f97c90e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9a3d677bf59b-0003-0002",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 68,
        "start": 68
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the U.S. Conference of Catholic Bishops, which calls it \"blatant religious discrimination.\""
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2017-17-965",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9a3d677bf59b0404b8933f001905d773fd9974778efe8dcbb9d5dd5b5f97c90e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9a3d677bf59b-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 69,
        "start": 68
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Number one is I think the very fact that this is immigration cuts the other way. I mean, the heart of the First Amendment is about immigration restrictions on, for example, Catholics at the founding and our protest of King George, which is all about using the immigration power to exclude people of a different faith. And that's what our Constitution is about. So that's the first thing."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "General Noel J. Francisco",
      "case_id": "2017-17-965",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9a3d677bf59b0404b8933f001905d773fd9974778efe8dcbb9d5dd5b5f97c90e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9a3d677bf59b-0003-0004",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 77,
        "start": 77
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The State Department does publish the waiver process on its website, but the waiver process actually is applied automatically by consular officers."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2017-17-965",
      "confidence": 0.0,
